      <!-- Description: executive summary or first key takeaway only (no full HTML body).
           This keeps the RSS file small and avoids duplicate-content issues with Google. -->
      <description><![CDATA[
        AlphaGenome 2 is here. By training on over 100 million single-cell profiles, this next-gen AI model predicts how DNA variants impact specific human cell types and disease states like never before.
        
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ The model was trained on more than 107 million individual cell profiles across 68 tissues, integrating bulk and single-cell data.
        [SPLIT]
        ⚡ It identifies nearly twice as many variants that alter gene expression in specialized cells compared to previous iterations.
        [SPLIT]
        🔗 Read full report → https://neodymium.world/articles/alphagenome-2-bridges-single-cell-biology-and-human-genetics-431152.html
